insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('34a24473-b030-5f2d-9ad1-2a10249571c8', 'rg5-theme-summary-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-theme-summary'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Game Over$q$, $q$For their technology project, Lucia and Dev had to build a simple video game together. Lucia wanted a game about a frog jumping across lily pads. Dev wanted a game about a rocket dodging asteroids.

"Mine is better," Dev said. "Rockets are exciting."

"Frogs are funny," Lucia said. "People like funny."

They could not agree, so each of them built a different game on the same laptop. On Thursday, the day before the project was due, the laptop froze. When they restarted it, both games crashed the moment they pressed Start.

Lucia put her head down on the desk. Dev stared at the screen.

After a minute, Dev said quietly, "My rocket code moves really well. Your lily pads look great. What if we only fix one game and use the best parts of both?"

Lucia lifted her head. "A frog that jumps across asteroids?"

Dev laughed. "A space frog."

They worked through lunch. Dev fixed the jumping code. Lucia drew a frog in a tiny space helmet. By the end of the day, the game ran without crashing.

On Friday, their classmates lined up to play Space Frog. Nobody remembered that it had started as two games.$q$, 'draft')
