   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Living history farms are more fun than any other kind of field trip.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Children two hundred years ago did not have to go to school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Bread tastes better when it is served on a farm than at home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Experiencing hard work can help people appreciate what they have.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Experiencing hard work can help people appreciate what they have.$q$, $q$After hauling water and churning butter, Tomas sets the table without complaining and smiles at the faucet. Mrs. Lindqvist says children did chores "before school, and after," so they did go to school.$q$, 'draft', 'f1c42eed-21e9-5053-b322-956d92a86509')
