   $q$How does Tomas's attitude at the beginning differ from his attitude at the end?$q$, $q$[{"text":"At first he loves farms, but at the end he wishes he had stayed home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-sequence"},{"text":"At first he dreads the trip, but at the end he is grateful for everyday comforts.","is_correct":true},{"text":"At first he is grateful, but at the end he complains about setting the table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-sequence"},{"text":"At first he is bored, and at the end he is still bored and tired.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-change"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At first he dreads the trip, but at the end he is grateful for everyday comforts.$q$, $q$Tomas groans about "a whole day without screens" and ends by doing his chore "without a word" and smiling. The choice "At first he is bored, and at the end he is still bored and tired" ignores that he clearly changes.$q$, 'draft', 'f1c42eed-21e9-5053-b322-956d92a86509')
