   $q$What topic is the speaker reflecting on in the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"How good things often take a long time and patience to grow.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Why fall is the most beautiful season of the whole year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Why neighbors should not tell others what to do in their yards.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"How to plant and water a maple tree in the right season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$How good things often take a long time and patience to grow.$q$, $q$The speaker connects the slow growth of the tree to "the best things" in life. The poem does not teach planting steps, so that choice confuses the subject with the message.$q$, 'draft', '5a896f5c-4474-5deb-981a-f9e2e84c2a08')
