   $q$Why does the poet include both the grandfather's actions and the speaker's thoughts?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show a lesson about patience being passed from one generation to the next.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain how much time it takes to dig a hole for a tree.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"To prove that only older people understand how trees grow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"To show that the speaker and the grandfather disagree about the tree.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show a lesson about patience being passed from one generation to the next.$q$, $q$The grandfather lived the lesson by caring for the tree, and the speaker says, "I am learning it this year." The speaker comes to agree with the grandfather, so they do not disagree.$q$, 'draft', '5a896f5c-4474-5deb-981a-f9e2e84c2a08')
